        "original_id": "bffb30ec-1841-51af-8770-eb27aa370e11",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Karl Dönitz, Lutz Graf Schwerin von Krosigk, Adolf Hitler, Hans-Georg von Friedeburg, Walter Warzecha\n- Organizations: Flensburg Government, Kriegsmarine\n- Roles: Reichspräsident, Leading Minister, Oberbefehlshaber der Kriegsmarine, head of state of Germany, Generaladmiral\n\nFacts:\n- Karl Dönitz briefly succeeded Adolf Hitler as the head of state of Germany.\n- The Flensburg Government was headed by Karl Dönitz as Reichspräsident and by Lutz Graf Schwerin von Krosigk as Leading Minister.\n- After the end of World War II, Walter Warzecha, serving as a General Admiral, succeeded Hans-Georg von Friedeburg as the last Oberbefehlshaber der Kriegsmarine.\n- Hans-Georg von Friedeburg committed suicide shortly after the dissolution of the Flensburg Government.",
